QuestGuidance.Register("en",83,{
[2625]="7000003E\n1\tDeliver Lily's letter to Candac\030Collect Letter to Candac\tCandac Brightwood is at the Forsaken Inn, east of the Midgewater Marshes along the Great East Road. Candac Brightwood supplies Lily Sandheaver with pottery and other collectibles from the ruins of the kingdom of Arnor. Lily gave you a letter for Candac and sent you to The Forsaken Inn to deliver it and inquire about the delay.\n",
[2626]="7000003F\n1\tDeliver bundled artifacts to Lily Sandheaver\tLily Sandheaver lives in her home at the corner of the road in Bree that leads up Bree-hill. Candac Brightwood, unable to pay a proper messenger, has asked you to make his most recent delivery to Lily Sandheaver.\n2\tDeliver the letter from Mrs. Sandheaver to Candac\tCandac Brightwood is at the Forsaken Inn, located on the Great East Road through the Lone-lands. Candac Brightwood sent you to deliver a bundle of old pottery to Lily Sandheaver, for which Mrs. Sandheaver paid you. You should return to Candac with the payment.\n",
[2627]="70000040\n1\tCollect pottery shards (total: 5)\tAncient bits of pottery may be found in the valley beneath the ruins of Minas Eriol, south-east of The Forsaken Inn. Candac Brightwood is at The Forsaken Inn. Candac Brightwood has asked you to search for bits of pottery with which he can continue his trade.\n2\tBring pottery shards to Candac Brightwood\tCandac Brightwood is at The Forsaken Inn. Candac Brightwood has asked you to search for bits of pottery with which he can continue his trade.\n",
[2628]="70060D82\n1\tFredegar's admirers can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should talk to Fredegar's admirers in order to get a better understanding of this hobbit's views.\t\n2\tTalk to Fredegar in Nobottle\tFredegar Bolger can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should talk to Fredegar Bolger.\n3\tDefeat ruffians in Yondershire (total: 8)\tRuffians can be found in the ruins of Ost Lagorath to the north and throughout Yondershire. Fredegar has asked you to defeat ruffians in Yondershire.\n4\tTalk to Fredegar in Nobottle\tFredegar Bolger can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should talk to Fredegar Bolger.\n5\tHobbits upset and disgruntled for various reasons can be found in villages throughout Yondershire. Fredegar has asked you to collect signatures from upset hobbits in each village.\t\n6\tTalk to Fredegar in Nobottle\tFredegar Bolger can be found in the village of Nobottle. You should bring the list of signatures to Fredegar Bolger.\n",
[2629]="7002F92C\n1\tTalk to Frithelm in Cliving\tCliving, the capital city of the Norcrofts, lies far to the north, beyond the trader's outpost along the road. Caddabrand has informed you that your share of the bounty may be collected from the warrior Frithelm, in Cliving.\n",
[2630]="70028442\n1\tDefeat the Captain of Fangs\tThe Captain of Fangs is in the stockade, north of Ondor. It can best be reached through the caves behind the stockade. Ondor has asked you to defeat the Captain of Fangs, a goblin Warg-rider of fierce renown and the leader of these goblins.\n2\tTalk to Ondor in Nan Curunír\tOndor is encamped south of the stockade. You should return to Ondor and tell him that the Captain of Fangs is no more.\n",
[2631]="7000874F\n1\tReturn to Chieftain Durulkum at Dâr-gazag\030Collect Captain-Generals' symbols (quantity: see journal)\tCaptain-Generals can only be found at locations where the enemy army holds power. Chieftain Durulkum directed you to collect Captain-General symbols from enemy leaders and then return to him.\n",
[2632]="700000B7\n1\tMeet Dawn Stockard to receive more Captain training\tDawn Stockard is in the town of Archet, north of Bree, in Bree-land. You have been told to speak with Dawn Stockard, a great captain, to learn what troubles her.\n2\tTalk to Dawn Stockard\tDawn Stockard is in the town of Archet, north of Bree, in Bree-land. You have been told to speak with Dawn Stockard, a great captain, to learn what troubles her.\n",
[2633]="700173A4\n1\tTalk to Garnyd at Anazârmekhem in the Flaming Deeps of Moria\tGarnyd is at Anazârmekhem in the Flaming Deeps of Moria. You have been instructed to seek out Captain Garnyd.\n2\tTalk to Garnyd at Anazârmekhem in the Flaming Deeps of Moria\tGarnyd is at Anazârmekhem in the Flaming Deeps of Moria. You have been instructed to seek out Captain Garnyd.\n",
[2634]="7000173A\n1\tDefeat Captain Shum-batar\030Defeat Captain Thorgal\030Defeat Captain Dombrî\tThe Ongbúrz captains Thorgal, Shum-batar, and Dombrî were last seen among the Warg-keepers in the Orc-camp in Dol Dínen, south-east of Esteldín. Elúr told you of the discovery of three captains of the Ongbúrz tribe who command the lower ranks of the Orc-host: Thorgal, Shum-batar, and Dombrî. He believes that their deaths will throw the lower ranks into confusion. He recommends you do not attempt this task alone.\n2\tReturn to Elúr\tElúr awaits word of your success at his encampment south-east of Esteldín. Elúr provided you the names of three Blogmal captains amongst the Orcs in Dol Dínen where the Warg-keepers patrol. With these captains slain, you should report back to Elúr.\n",
[2635]="7004429C\n1\tDefeat Burgúl\030Defeat Vordugúr\030Defeat Jagai\tThe high ranking captains of the Morgul-host can be found in Pelennor Fields. You should defeat these high ranking captains.\n2\tSpeak with Turgon\tTurgon can be found at the South-gate of the Rammas. You should speak with Turgon.\n",
[2636]="700544A9\n1\tFree caged spirits (total: 12)\tCaged spirits can be found in the Circle of Sorrow in Minas Morgul. You should set the caged spirits free.\n2\tTalk to Dolenthol in Barad Orhant\tDolenthol can be found in Barad Orhant. You should talk to Dolenthol.\n",
[2637]="70017AEA\n1\tCapture an outpost in the Ettenmoors\tMake your way into the Ettenmoors and seek one of the outposts there. These can be found in the far south-west, overlooking the river near Hoarhallow, the near south north-west just beyond the river and north near the western entrance of the Isendeep Mine. You have been tasked with capturing an outpost within the Ettenmoors. You should return to War-tyrant Akulhún when this is complete.\n2\tReturn to War-tyrant Akulhún at Gramsfoot\tThe outpost is claimed for Angmar. Return to War-tyrant Akulhún at Gramsfoot and tell him of your victory.\n",
[2638]="70017AEB\n1\tCapture an outpost in the Ettenmoors\tMake your way into the Ettenmoors and seek one of the outposts there. These can be found in the far south-west, overlooking the river near Hoarhallow, the near south north-west just beyond the river and north near the western entrance of the Isendeep Mine. You have been tasked with capturing an outpost within the Ettenmoors. You should return to Captain-General Tordúr when this is complete.\n2\tReturn to Captain-General Tordúr at Glân Vraig\tThe outpost is claimed for the Free People. Return to Glân Vraig and inform Captain-General Tordúr of your victory.\n",
[2639]="7002827A\n1\tCollect food-stores (total: 5)\tThe stolen food can be found at Lhan Gogledh, north of Lhucu's hut. Lhucu has asked you to recover the stolen food for the people of Lhan Bach.\n2\tTalk to Lhucu at her hut\tLhucu is at her hut, south of Lhan Gogledh. You should bring the food-stores to Lhucu so that she may redistribute them to the people of Lhan Bach.\n",
[2640]="700529DB\n1\tCollect crayfish traps (total: 8)\tCrayfish traps can be found along the Anduin River in Duskenvale. You should collect the crayfish traps.\n2\tTalk to Tassila\tTassila can be found at the river docks in Arhaim. You should bring the trout to Tassila.\n",
[2641]="7004A8E4\n1\tCaptured Men can be found in the Tower of Cirith Ungol. Legolas has asked you to rescue the Men taken into the Tower by Captain Róglarg's garrison.\t\n2\tCompleted\tYou have freed many of the captured Men from the Tower of Cirith Ungol.\n",
[2642]="7005403F\n1\tCaptured soldiers are being held by the Enemy in Parth Daenath. You should free any captured soldiers that you find.\t\n2\tTalk to Celeborn\tCeleborn can be found at Echad-in-Edhil. You should talk to Celeborn.\n",
[2643]="70040416\n1\tRescue the kidnapped townsfolk\tVillagers can be found trapped inside their home in Lothgobel, in central Lamedon. You should free the villagers who were left behind.\n2\tVillagers can be found trapped inside their home in Lothgobel, in central Lamedon. You should free the villagers who were left behind.\t\n3\tCompleted\tYou have freed the kidnapped townsfolk from their overrun home in Lothgobel.\n",
[2644]="70015E09\n1\tFind Thorlák\tThorlák entered the Redhorn Gate in search of Durin's Tower in the eastern parts of the pass, upon Zirakzigil. Hjór hopes that Thorlák has found some shelter in the upper reaches of the Redhorn Gate.\n2\tTalk to Hjór at Echad Dúnann\tHjór is in Echad Dúnann, south-west of the Redhorn Gate. You should return to Hjór and inform him of Thorlák's death.\n",
[2645]="70062E7B\n1\tDefeat Caranost warriors (total: 10)\tCaranost warriors can be found west of Sírlond, throughout the city.\n2\tTalk to Sirvellon at Sírlond\tSirvellon is at his camp of Sírlond, east of Caranost proper.\n",
[2646]="70063CC8\n1\tDeliver the blackened furs to a collection box\030Collect blackened furs (total: 10)\tYou have accepted a task to acquire blackened furs.\n",
